From 1a687fa93552944336ff6e8fe48c18e6863f6e11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 12:41:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 141/145] media: meson: vdec: enable MPEG-4, H.263 and VC-1 on
 the remaining platforms

MPEG-4 Part 2, H.263 and VC-1 were wired up on G12A only, as the parts
they were developed and tested on.  Nothing about them is G12-specific:
all three run on VDEC_1 through codec_mpeg4_ops and codec_vc1_ops,
neither of which contains a single revision-dependent register write,
and the microcode the G12A entries load for MPEG-4 and H.263 is the GX
build already.

Wire them up on gxbb, gxl, gxlx, gxm and sm1 with the same geometry and
buffer counts G12A uses.  VC-1 takes the GX microcode on the GX parts;
sm1 takes the G12A build, which is also where its H.264 entry gets its
firmware.

Untested on every platform this adds them to - the codecs carry no
per-SoC code, so the risk is entirely in whether each microcode build
runs on each part.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
